  data:  # e88f
    kind: work_item  # e88f
    title: "Session-bus/keyring daemons leaked by gh auth token exhausted the per-user inotify limit; transcript watchers outlived their sessions (session crash 2026-09-05)"  # e88f
    status: todo_hard  # e88f
    priority: 2  # e88f
    parent:  # e88f
    tags:  # e88f
    - agent_infrastructure  # e88f
    - hooks  # e88f
    - transcript_pipeline  # e88f
    isbefore: []  # e88f
    duplicate_of: []  # e88f
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e88f
    pr_ref: '#782'  # e88f
    description: "CLASS: a process the harness or a hook starts must not outlive the session that started it, and a resource with a per-user cap (inotify instances, 128) must not be consumed by processes nobody owns.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED (2026-09-05). The Claude Code session crashed at 05:46Z, idle, three minutes after a turn ended. Diagnosis found the per-user inotify instance limit at 128/128 — `inotify_init` returned EMFILE (\"Too many open files\") from inside the next session, and that session's harness process held zero inotify instances, i.e. its file watching had failed at startup. Node crashes on exactly that error when it tries to watch a file. dmesg was not readable; the harness left no log; this is the only abnormal condition found and it is chronic — the journal shows \"Cannot initialize inotify\" since at least Aug 1.\n\nTWO LEAKS held the 128:\n(1) 126 instances: orphaned `dbus-daemon --session` processes (265 alive, each paired with a `gnome-keyring-daemon`, all reparented to PID 1, accumulating 13–73/day since the Aug 29 boot; 404 spawned since Aug 28). Every one was spawned by `gh auth token` (295× `--hostname github.com`, 107× bare): the box is headless with no session bus and gh had NO stored credential (~/.config/gh absent, `gh auth status` exit 1), so each call reached for the OS keyring over D-Bus, autolaunched a bus + keyring daemon, and left both running forever. The caller is the harness itself (two pairs appear at every session start, 12 s before the first transcript entry; no repo hook or script invokes `gh auth token`). Sessions in ~/ethical.superintelligence produced most of them by volume — via the harness, not that repo's code.\n(2) 2 instances: hypergumbo's own transcript watcher. A 50-hour `inotifywait -e close_write` with PPID 1 (its bash took an untrapped SIGTERM and died, leaving the untimed foreground child) and a 26-hour sync-transcript.sh in Phase 1 for a source that never appeared (the crashed session never ran its session-end hook).\n\nFIXES.\n- Machine (owner-authorised): killed the 530 orphan processes by explicit PID (list in the session scratchpad); `gh auth login --with-token --insecure-storage` from .env so gh never touches the keyring — first with the token then in .env, which resolved to josh-iterabloom (the human), then re-done after the owner minted a PAT on the jgstern-agent account and replaced HG_GITHUB_TOKEN; the human account was logged out of gh's store. Positive control: `gh auth token`, `gh auth status`, `gh api user`, `gh pr list` each spawn nothing (before the fix one call spawned one pair). Note: HG_GITHUB_TOKEN had been the human's token — every PR the agent opened via auto-pr showed as created by josh-iterabloom (e.g. #779); git pushes were already jgstern-agent via SSH. PR #782 was the first merged as jgstern-agent (push+maintain, no admin).\n- Repo: PR #782 — every inotifywait carries -t (TRANSCRIPT_WATCH_TIMEOUT, default 60 s); the watch runs under `wait` with TERM/INT/HUP trapped so the handler reaps the child; launch-transcript-sync.sh names the owner in TRANSCRIPT_OWNER_PID (CLAUDE_PID, else first non-shell ancestor) and both phases check it every iteration by PID and /proc start time; kill-transcript-sync.sh signals children before the watcher. Nine tests in tests/test_watcher_lifecycle.py.\n\nVERIFIED AFTER: inotify instances in use 1/128; `inotify_init` succeeds; 1 real session bus (sddm's), 0 keyring daemons; both pre-fix watcher orphans killed by PID.\n\nRESIDUAL / NOT DONE: the harness process of the diagnosing session still holds 0 watchers (needs a restart to be fully clean). The leak trigger is external to this repo (the harness calling gh on a box with no stored credential); the repo has no guard that would have surfaced 128/128 or an unauthenticated gh at session start — see the sibling proposal item. `fs.inotify.max_user_instances` remains 128 (root needed to raise). Session 82cef451's watcher had no source transcript at all — why that session produced none is unexplained."  # e88f
    fields: {}  # e88f
